1
00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:09.680
This video demonstrates how to perform a front of the eye examination using the

2
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.900
anterior segment loop of the Arclight device.

3
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.406
Start with hand hygiene and introduce yourself.

4
00:00:17.406 --> 00:00:24.920
Confirm the identity of the patient, explain the examination, and gain consent to perform it.

5
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:29.470
Initially take a few seconds to observe both eyes at the same time.

6
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.920
Look at the periorbitor, eyelids and eyes.

7
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.160
Commenting on any swelling, redness and discharge, as well as prominence of the eyes or abnormal

8
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.680
eyelid position.

9
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.608
Then perform a magnified examination using the arc light.

10
00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:45.560
Switch on the white light and

11
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.679
hold the device close to your eye.

12
00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:50.100
Slowly approach the patient's right eye first until

13
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.220
it is in focus.

14
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.900
This will be at around 6cm.

15
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.420
As the patient to move their eye outwards and

16
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.749
inwards, then up and down, while gently holding their eyelids.

17
00:00:58.749 --> 00:01:00.080
Systematically noting a different

18
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.675
structures seen, thinking of them in groups.

19
00:01:02.675 --> 00:01:05.640
The first group includes the upper and lower

20
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.432
eyelashes and lid margins.

21
00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:16.110
The second includes a conjunctiva and sclera and the lower forenicks.

22
00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:20.425
The third group is the cornea, the junction of this with a sclera called

23
00:01:20.425 --> 00:01:21.350
the limbis and

24
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.579
the pupil, surrounded by the iris.

25
00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:26.550
Once you've finished noting all these structures, now

26
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.190
Now select the blue light on the arc light.

27
00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:34.310
With fluorescing dye, the tear film, areas of epithelial loss and disease will be highlighted.

28
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.270
The dye fluoresces brightly with the blue light.

29
00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.430
Record on a diagram the sight and size of areas of epithelial loss and disease.

30
00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.410
Finish by examining the superior tarsal plate.

31
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.030
Place a cotton bud on the upper lid, then gently lift the lashes upwards while slowly

32
00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.550
pressing downwards with the bud.

33
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:57.562
observed with a naked eye, then bring in the arc light for a magnified view.

34
00:01:57.562 --> 00:01:58.230
Repeat this

35
00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.130
examination on the other eye.

36
00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:03.550
Afterwards, thank the patient, summarise and record your findings

37
00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:04.614
and repeat hand hygiene.

38
00:02:04.614 --> 00:02:08.070
Please have a look at our other University of St Andrews Arc Light

